Without a profile:
every Search_shaping key has a registered default, spelled so its own kind parses it: true
the registry names no key outside the Search_shaping class: true
with every Search_shaping key unset or at its default, the identity is empty: true
each Search_shaping key stated at its default, spelled otherwise, leaves the identity alone: true
each Search_shaping key stated off its default renders, canonically spelled: true
an unparsable value renders as stated: true
where the lanes' scalar recompute is cheap, auto is the cooperative preamble and cut lanes: true
and there the refused preamble, admitted lanes and one simdgroup are not the default: true
where it is costly, auto is the refused preamble and admitted lanes, and the reverse renders: true
a block size the device clamps to the default's clamp is the default, unclamped it renders: true
an explicit mode renders as the device resolves it: true
a read whose default means the registered value is served, in any spelling: true
a read whose default means another value is refused: true
Under the commandline-picked profile performance:
the performance profile sets the beam width off its default and the search at it: true
the commandline restores the rounds the profile raises to their built-in default: true
the identity is the profile's off-default value alone, as a profile-less statement of it would render: true
